`cast` converts a value to the type required by its immediate typed
destination:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    count U64 = cast 42
    label String = cast count
]

The destination must already give a concrete type. An untyped binding cannot
supply one:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    invalid = cast source
]

Use `catch` to handle a fallible conversion and any failure while evaluating
its operand:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    count I32 = cast text catch then 0
]

There is no cast-specific propagation spelling. A fallible cast follows the
ordinary implicit or typed error route. Postfix `!` still applies to ordinary
fallible calls. See @./#cast-syntax (Cast syntax) for target boundaries and
source inference barriers.
